From a925511682993012145e95a0bea2fb1ac8aa8605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grearjake-star <228037169+grearjake-star@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:57:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] perf(cuda): EXL3 prompt experts decode each weight tile
 once for up to 64 pairs (same bits)

Prompt windows of the routed EXL3 experts ran the grouping kernel, whose grid spans every (expert slot, 16-pair
tile) of the window - nearly all empty at prompt sizes - and decodes each trellis tile again for every 16 pairs,
writing fp32 split-K partials for an epilogue to sum. Above 64 rows, routed() now groups pairs on
tensorfold.cuda.experts' plan (items of <= 64 pairs of one expert) and runs experts_prompt.cuh: a program
(64-column block, item, matrix) decodes its tiles into shared memory a chunk at a time for its four 16-pair
member tiles, A arrives by cp.async and leaves by ldmatrix, and each pair runs grouped_kernel's arithmetic
over the whole K: the same m16n8k16 chains over the same K segments, segments added in warp order, splits
added from 0. Gate|up leave one final sum; down owns a 128-column Hadamard block and runs down_epilogue's
arithmetic itself, storing Y as fp32 or once-rounded into y_out. One instance per bit width; a layer launches
the widths it holds. Decode windows keep the grouping kernel; TF_EXL3_PROMPT=group keeps it everywhere.

Qwen3.8 Flash Next EXL3 4.05 (GB10, real routing of a 2K chunk): a layer's routed experts over 1,024 rows
25.1 -> 7.7 ms. tests/cuda/test_exl3_prompt_experts.py: every codebook, mixed widths, skewed routing, skipped
picks, the combine, bf16 Y, a row alone == the row in a window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
